#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Overview {#overview}"
msgstr "Pangkalahatang-ideya {#overview}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Partial Differential Equation (PDE) solver presented here is part of our Quantum Innovative Computing Kit (QUICK) platform (QUICK-PDE), and is packaged as a Quantum Function. With the QUICK-PDE function, you can solve domain-specific partial differential equations on IBM Quantum QPUs. This function is based on the algorithm described in [ColibriTD's H-DES description paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/2410.01130). This algorithm can solve complex multi-physics problems, starting with Computational Fluid Dynamics (CFD) and Materials Deformation (MD), and now including quantitative finance with the Black-Scholes equation for options on one to three assets. Other use cases are coming soon.\n"
msgstr "Ang Partial Differential Equation (PDE) solver na ipinapakita dito ay bahagi ng aming Quantum Innovative Computing Kit (QUICK) platform (QUICK-PDE), at nakabalot bilang isang Quantum Function. Sa pamamagitan ng QUICK-PDE function, maaari kang maglutas ng domain-specific partial differential equations sa IBM Quantum QPUs. Ang function na ito ay nakabatay sa algorithm na inilalarawan sa [papel ng ColibriTD na naglalarawan sa H-DES](https://arxiv.org/abs/2410.01130). Kaya ng algorithm na ito na harapin ang mga kumplikadong multi-physics na problema, simula sa Computational Fluid Dynamics (CFD) at Materials Deformation (MD), at ngayon ay kasama na ang quantitative finance gamit ang Black-Scholes equation para sa mga option sa isa hanggang tatlong asset. May iba pang use case na paparating.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To tackle the differential equations, the trial solutions are encoded as linear combinations of orthogonal functions (typically Chebyshev polynomials, and more specifically up to $2^n$ of them where $n$ is the number of qubits encoding your function), parametrized by the angles of a Variable Quantum Circuit (VQC). The ansatz generates a state encoding the function, which is evaluated by observables whose combinations allow for evaluating the function at all points. You can then evaluate the loss function in which the differential equations are encoded, and fine-tune the angles in a hybrid loop, as shown in the following. The trial solutions get gradually closer to the actual solutions until you reach a satisfactory result.\n"
msgstr "Para harapin ang mga differential equations, ang mga trial solution ay naka-encode bilang linear combinations ng mga orthogonal function (karaniwang Chebyshev polynomials, at mas partikular na hanggang $2^n$ sa kanila kung saan ang $n$ ay ang bilang ng mga qubit na nag-e-encode ng iyong function), na naka-parametrize sa pamamagitan ng mga anggulo ng isang Variable Quantum Circuit (VQC). Ang ansatz ay bumubuo ng isang estado na nag-e-encode ng function, na sinusuri ng mga observable na ang kombinasyon nito ay nagbibigay-daan sa pag-evaluate ng function sa lahat ng punto. Maaari kang mag-evaluate ng loss function kung saan naka-encode ang mga differential equations, at i-fine-tune ang mga anggulo sa isang hybrid loop, tulad ng ipinapakita sa sumusunod. Ang mga trial solution ay unti-unting lumalapit sa mga aktwal na solusyon hanggang sa makamit mo ang kasiya-siyang resulta.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Workflow of the QUICK-PDE function](/docs/images/guides/colibritd-equation-solver/diagram.svg)\n"
msgstr "![Daloy ng trabaho ng QUICK-PDE function](/docs/images/guides/colibritd-equation-solver/diagram.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In addition to this hybrid loop, you can also chain together different optimizers. This is useful when you want a global optimizer to find a good set of angles, and then a more fine-tuned optimizer to follow a gradient to the best set of neighboring angles. In the case of computational fluid dynamics (CFD), the default optimization sequence produces the best results - but in the case of material deformation (MD), while the default provides good results, you can configure it further for problem-specific benefits.\n"
msgstr "Bukod sa hybrid loop na ito, maaari ka ring mag-chain ng iba't ibang optimizer. Ito ay kapaki-pakinabang kapag gusto mong gamitin ang isang global optimizer para mahanap ang magandang set ng mga anggulo, at pagkatapos ay isang mas pinong optimizer para sundan ang gradient patungo sa pinakamahusay na set ng kalapit na mga anggulo. Sa kaso ng computational fluid dynamics (CFD), ang default na optimization sequence ay nagbibigay ng pinakamahusay na resulta — ngunit sa kaso ng material deformation (MD), habang nagbibigay ng magandang resulta ang default, maaari mo itong i-configure pa para sa mga benepisyong partikular sa problema.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Note that for each variable of the function, you specify the number of qubits (which you can experiment with). By stacking 10 identical circuits and evaluating the 10 identical observables on different qubits throughout one big circuit, you can noise-mitigate within the CMA optimization process or parallelize the PSR computations, relying on the noise learner method, and significantly reducing the number of shots needed.\n"
msgstr "Tandaan na para sa bawat variable ng function, tinutukoy mo ang bilang ng mga qubit (na maaari mong subukan-subukan). Sa pag-stack ng 10 magkaparehong circuit at pag-evaluate ng 10 magkaparehong observable sa iba't ibang qubit sa buong isang malaking circuit, maaari kang mag-noise-mitigate sa loob ng proseso ng CMA optimization o i-parallelize ang mga PSR computation, umaasa sa noise learner method, at makabuluhang binabawasan ang bilang ng mga shot na kailangan.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Computational fluid dynamics {#computational-fluid-dynamics}"
msgstr "Computational fluid dynamics {#computational-fluid-dynamics}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**The inviscid Burgers' equation** models flowing non-viscous fluids as follows:\n"
msgstr "**Ang inviscid Burgers' equation** ay nagmo-modelo ng daloy ng mga di-malapot na likido tulad ng sumusunod:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial t} + u\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial x} = 0$,\n"
msgstr "$\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial t} + u\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial x} = 0$,\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$u$ represents the fluid speed field. This use-case has a temporal boundary condition: you can select the initial condition and then allow the system to relax. Currently, the only accepted initial conditions are linear functions: $ax + b$. The analytical solution is:\n"
msgstr "Ang $u$ ay kumakatawan sa field ng bilis ng likido. Ang use case na ito ay may temporal na boundary condition: maaari kang pumili ng initial condition at hayaan ang sistema na mag-relax. Sa kasalukuyan, ang mga tanging tinatanggap na initial condition ay mga linear function: $ax + b$. Ang analytical solution ay:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$u(t, x) = \\frac{ax + b}{at + 1}$.\n"
msgstr "$u(t, x) = \\frac{ax + b}{at + 1}$.\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**The pressureless Euler equations** model compressible inviscid fluid flow with damping as follows:\n"
msgstr "**Ang pressureless Euler equations** ay nagmo-modelo ng compressible inviscid fluid flow na may damping tulad ng sumusunod:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$\\frac{\\partial g}{\\partial t} + u\\frac{\\partial g}{\\partial x} + g\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial x} = 0$,\n"
msgstr "$\\frac{\\partial g}{\\partial t} + u\\frac{\\partial g}{\\partial x} + g\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial x} = 0$,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$u\\frac{\\partial g}{\\partial t} + g\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial t} + u^2\\frac{\\partial g}{\\partial x} + 2gu\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial x} + \\frac{\\mu}{(1+t)^{\\lambda}} g u = 0$,\n"
msgstr "$u\\frac{\\partial g}{\\partial t} + g\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial t} + u^2\\frac{\\partial g}{\\partial x} + 2gu\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial x} + \\frac{\\mu}{(1+t)^{\\lambda}} g u = 0$,\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$g$ represents the density field, $u$ the velocity field and $\\mu$ a damping coefficient. In our formulation, we pose $\\lambda = 1$, so it will not be used as a parameter in the following. This use-case has temporal boundary conditions: $g(0, x) = e^{-x}$ and $u(0, x) = x$. The analytical solution is:\n"
msgstr "Ang $g$ ay kumakatawan sa density field, ang $u$ sa velocity field at ang $\\mu$ sa isang damping coefficient. Sa ating formulation, itinakda natin na $\\lambda = 1$, kaya hindi ito gagamitin bilang parameter sa sumusunod. Ang use-case na ito ay may temporal boundary conditions: $g(0, x) = e^{-x}$ at $u(0, x) = x$. Ang analytical solution ay:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$g(t, x) = \\frac{1-\\mu}{(1+t)^{1-\\mu} - \\mu} \\exp\\!\\left(\\frac{(\\mu-1)\\, x}{(1+t)^{1-\\mu} - \\mu}\\right)$,\n"
msgstr "$g(t, x) = \\frac{1-\\mu}{(1+t)^{1-\\mu} - \\mu} \\exp\\!\\left(\\frac{(\\mu-1)\\, x}{(1+t)^{1-\\mu} - \\mu}\\right)$,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$u(t, x) = \\frac{(1-\\mu)\\, x}{\\left((1+t)^{1-\\mu} - \\mu\\right)(1+t)^{\\mu}}$.\n"
msgstr "$u(t, x) = \\frac{(1-\\mu)\\, x}{\\left((1+t)^{1-\\mu} - \\mu\\right)(1+t)^{\\mu}}$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The arguments for CFD's differential equations are on a fixed grid, as follows:\n"
msgstr "Ang mga argumento para sa mga differential equation ng CFD ay nasa isang fixed grid, tulad ng sumusunod:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "$t$ is between 0 and 0.95 with 41 sample points. $x$ is between 0 and 0.95 with 41 sample points.\n"
msgstr "Ang $t$ ay nasa pagitan ng 0 at 0.95 na may 41 sample points. Ang $x$ ay nasa pagitan ng 0 at 0.95 na may 41 sample points.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Material deformation {#material-deformation}"
msgstr "Material Deformation {#material-deformation}"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This use case focuses on **hypoelastic deformation with the one-dimensional tensile test**, in which a bar fixed in space is pulled at its other extremity. We describe the problem as follows:\n"
msgstr "Ang use case na ito ay nakatuon sa hypoelastic deformation na may one-dimensional tensile test, kung saan ang isang bar na nakapirmi sa espasyo ay hinihila sa kabilang dulo nito. Inilalarawan namin ang problema tulad ng sumusunod:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$u' - \\frac{\\sigma}{3K} - \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}\\epsilon_0\\left(\\frac{\\sigma'}{\\sigma_0\\sqrt{3}}\\right)^n = 0$,\n"
msgstr "$u' - \\frac{\\sigma}{3K} - \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}\\epsilon_0\\left(\\frac{\\sigma'}{\\sigma_0\\sqrt{3}}\\right)^n = 0$,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$\\sigma' - b = 0$,\n"
msgstr "$\\sigma' - b = 0$,\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$K$ represents the bulk modulus of the material being stretched, $n$ the exponent of a power law, $b$ the force per unit mass, $\\epsilon_0$ the proportional stress limit, $\\sigma_0$ the proportional strain limit, $u$ the stress function, and $\\sigma$ the strain function. The analytical solution is:\n"
msgstr "Ang $K$ ay kumakatawan sa bulk modulus ng materyal na iniuunat, ang $n$ ang exponent ng isang power law, ang $b$ ang puwersa bawat unit mass, ang $\\epsilon_0$ ang proportional stress limit, ang $\\sigma_0$ ang proportional strain limit, ang $u$ ang stress function, at ang $\\sigma$ ang strain function. Ang analytical solution ay:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$\\sigma(x) = \\sigma_0 - bx$,\n"
msgstr "$\\sigma(x) = \\sigma_0 - bx$,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$u(x) = -\\frac{3^{-(3+n)/2}}{2bK(1+n)\\,\\sigma_0^{n}}\\Biggl[3^{(1+n)/2}b^2\\sigma_0^n(1+n)x^2 - 2\\cdot 3^{(1+n)/2}b\\sigma_0^n(1+n)\\sigma_0 x - 12\\epsilon_0 K\\sigma_0^{1+n}$\n"
"$- 12b\\epsilon_0 K\\sigma_0^n x\\left(\\frac{-bx+\\sigma_0}{\\sigma_0}\\right)^n + 12\\epsilon_0 K\\sigma_0^{n+1}\\left(\\frac{-bx+\\sigma_0}{\\sigma_0}\\right)^n - 12\\epsilon_0 K \\sigma_0^{1+n}\\Biggr]$,\n"
msgstr ""
"$u(x) = -\\frac{3^{-(3+n)/2}}{2bK(1+n)\\,\\sigma_0^{n}}\\Biggl[3^{(1+n)/2}b^2\\sigma_0^n(1+n)x^2 - 2\\cdot 3^{(1+n)/2}b\\sigma_0^n(1+n)\\sigma_0 x - 12\\epsilon_0 K\\sigma_0^{1+n}$\n"
"$- 12b\\epsilon_0 K\\sigma_0^n x\\left(\\frac{-bx+\\sigma_0}{\\sigma_0}\\right)^n + 12\\epsilon_0 K\\sigma_0^{n+1}\\left(\\frac{-bx+\\sigma_0}{\\sigma_0}\\right)^n - 12\\epsilon_0 K \\sigma_0^{1+n}\\Biggr]$,\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where $\\sigma_0 = g(0)$ is the boundary condition on the strain at $x=0$.\n"
msgstr "kung saan ang $\\sigma_0 = g(0)$ ay ang boundary condition sa strain sa $x=0$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The considered bar is of unitary length. This use-case has a boundary condition for surface stress $t$, or the amount of work needed to stretch the bar.\n"
msgstr "Ang isinasaalang-alang na bar ay may unitary na haba. Ang use case na ito ay may boundary condition para sa surface stress $t$, o ang dami ng trabahong kailangan para maunat ang bar.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The arguments for MD's differential equations are on a fixed grid, as follows:\n"
msgstr "Ang mga argumento para sa mga differential equation ng MD ay nasa isang fixed grid, tulad ng sumusunod:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "$x$ is between 0 and 1 with 30 sample points.\n"
msgstr "Ang $x$ ay nasa pagitan ng 0 at 1 na may 30 sample points.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Quantitative finance {#quantitative-finance}"
msgstr "Quantitative finance {#quantitative-finance}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**The Black-Scholes equation** gives the price $C$ of a European call option as a function of the time $t$ and of the price of the underlying asset or assets. We pose a zero interest rate, no dividends and a maturity $T = 1$. This use case is available for one, two and three assets.\n"
msgstr "**Ang Black-Scholes equation** ay nagbibigay ng presyo $C$ ng isang European call option bilang function ng oras $t$ at ng presyo ng underlying asset o mga asset. Nagtatakda kami ng zero interest rate, walang dividend at maturity na $T = 1$. Available ang use case na ito para sa isa, dalawa at tatlong asset.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For a single asset, the equation reads:\n"
msgstr "Para sa isang asset, ganito ang equation:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$\\frac{\\partial C}{\\partial t} + \\frac{\\sigma^2}{2} S^2 \\frac{\\partial^2 C}{\\partial S^2} = 0$,\n"
msgstr "$\\frac{\\partial C}{\\partial t} + \\frac{\\sigma^2}{2} S^2 \\frac{\\partial^2 C}{\\partial S^2} = 0$,\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where $\\sigma$ is the volatility of the asset and $S$ its price. The boundary conditions are given by the analytical solution. It fixes the price at the final time $t = 0.9$ (a residual maturity of 0.1) and at the edges $S = 1$ and $S = 2$ of the price domain, and the solver recovers the price at the earlier times. The analytical solution is:\n"
msgstr "kung saan ang $\\sigma$ ay ang volatility ng asset at ang $S$ ang presyo nito. Ibinibigay ng analytical solution ang mga boundary condition. Itinatakda nito ang presyo sa huling oras na $t = 0.9$ (natitirang maturity na 0.1) at sa mga gilid na $S = 1$ at $S = 2$ ng price domain, at binabawi ng solver ang presyo sa mga naunang oras. Ang analytical solution ay:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$C(t, S) = S\\,\\Phi(d_1) - K\\,\\Phi(d_2), \\qquad d_{1,2} = \\frac{\\ln(S/K) \\pm \\frac{\\sigma^2}{2}(T-t)}{\\sigma\\sqrt{T-t}}$,\n"
msgstr "$C(t, S) = S\\,\\Phi(d_1) - K\\,\\Phi(d_2), \\qquad d_{1,2} = \\frac{\\ln(S/K) \\pm \\frac{\\sigma^2}{2}(T-t)}{\\sigma\\sqrt{T-t}}$,\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where $K$ is the strike of the option and $\\Phi$ is the cumulative distribution function of the standard normal distribution.\n"
msgstr "kung saan ang $K$ ay ang strike ng option at ang $\\Phi$ ay ang cumulative distribution function ng standard normal distribution.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For **baskets of two and three assets**, the option is written on the geometric average $G = \\prod_{i=1}^{n} S_i^{w_i}$ of the $n$ asset prices, where the weights $w_i$ are strictly positive and sum to 1:\n"
msgstr "Para sa **mga basket ng dalawa at tatlong asset**, isinusulat ang option sa geometric average na $G = \\prod_{i=1}^{n} S_i^{w_i}$ ng $n$ presyo ng asset, kung saan mahigpit na positibo ang mga weight na $w_i$ at ang kabuuan ay 1:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$\\frac{\\partial C}{\\partial t} + \\sum_{i=1}^{n} \\frac{\\sigma_i^2}{2} S_i^2 \\frac{\\partial^2 C}{\\partial S_i^2} + \\sum_{i<j} \\rho_{ij}\\,\\sigma_i\\sigma_j\\, S_i S_j \\frac{\\partial^2 C}{\\partial S_i \\partial S_j} = 0$,\n"
msgstr "$\\frac{\\partial C}{\\partial t} + \\sum_{i=1}^{n} \\frac{\\sigma_i^2}{2} S_i^2 \\frac{\\partial^2 C}{\\partial S_i^2} + \\sum_{i<j} \\rho_{ij}\\,\\sigma_i\\sigma_j\\, S_i S_j \\frac{\\partial^2 C}{\\partial S_i \\partial S_j} = 0$,\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where $\\sigma_i$ is the volatility of asset $i$ and $\\rho_{ij}$ the correlation between assets $i$ and $j$. The boundary conditions are given by the analytical solution on the final time and on the edges of the price domain. With $\\tau = T - t$, the analytical solution is:\n"
msgstr "kung saan ang $\\sigma_i$ ay ang volatility ng asset na $i$ at ang $\\rho_{ij}$ ang correlation ng mga asset na $i$ at $j$. Ibinibigay ng analytical solution ang mga boundary condition sa huling oras at sa mga gilid ng price domain. Kapag $\\tau = T - t$, ang analytical solution ay:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$C = G\\,e^{-q\\tau}\\,\\Phi(d_1) - K\\,\\Phi(d_2), \\qquad d_1 = \\frac{\\ln(G/K) + \\left(\\frac{\\sigma_G^2}{2} - q\\right)\\tau}{\\sigma_G\\sqrt{\\tau}}, \\qquad d_2 = d_1 - \\sigma_G\\sqrt{\\tau}$,\n"
msgstr "$C = G\\,e^{-q\\tau}\\,\\Phi(d_1) - K\\,\\Phi(d_2), \\qquad d_1 = \\frac{\\ln(G/K) + \\left(\\frac{\\sigma_G^2}{2} - q\\right)\\tau}{\\sigma_G\\sqrt{\\tau}}, \\qquad d_2 = d_1 - \\sigma_G\\sqrt{\\tau}$,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$\\sigma_G^2 = \\sum_{i} w_i^2\\sigma_i^2 + 2\\sum_{i<j} \\rho_{ij}\\, w_i w_j\\, \\sigma_i\\sigma_j, \\qquad q = \\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\sum_i w_i\\sigma_i^2 - \\sigma_G^2\\right)$,\n"
msgstr "$\\sigma_G^2 = \\sum_{i} w_i^2\\sigma_i^2 + 2\\sum_{i<j} \\rho_{ij}\\, w_i w_j\\, \\sigma_i\\sigma_j, \\qquad q = \\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\sum_i w_i\\sigma_i^2 - \\sigma_G^2\\right)$,\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "and the one-asset solution is recovered for $n = 1$ and $w_1 = 1$.\n"
msgstr "at nababawi ang solusyon para sa isang asset kapag $n = 1$ at $w_1 = 1$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The physical parameters of the use case are the following:\n"
msgstr "Ang mga pisikal na parameter ng use case ay ang mga sumusunod:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Parameter                             | Description                                                                                                   | Range                                                          | Business range                                                                  |\n"
"| ------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| `sigma`, `sigma1`, `sigma2`, `sigma3` | Volatility of each asset                                                                                      | 0.05 to 1                                                      | 0.10 to 0.40                                                                    |\n"
"| `K`                                   | Strike of the option                                                                                          | 1 to 2                                                         | 1.2 to 1.8 (80% to 120% of a spot price at the center of the domain, $S = 1.5$) |\n"
"| `w1` (basket of 2 assets)             | Weight of the first asset. The weight of the second asset is deduced: $w_2 = 1 - w_1$                         | Each weight is strictly positive (so $0 < w_1 < 1$)            | Each weight from 0.2 to 0.8                                                     |\n"
"| `w1`, `w2` (basket of 3 assets)       | Weights of the first and of the second asset. The weight of the third asset is deduced: $w_3 = 1 - w_1 - w_2$ | Each weight is strictly positive (so $w_1 + w_2 < 1$)          | Each of the three weights from 0.2 to 0.8                                       |\n"
"| `rho`, `rho12`, `rho13`, `rho23`      | Correlation between two assets                                                                                | 0 to 1 (the correlation matrix must be positive semi-definite) | 0.1 to 0.8                                                                      |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Parameter                             | Paglalarawan                                                                                                  | Saklaw                                                         | Business range                                                                  |\n"
"| ------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| `sigma`, `sigma1`, `sigma2`, `sigma3` | Volatility ng bawat asset                                                                                     | 0.05 hanggang 1                                                | 0.10 hanggang 0.40                                                              |\n"
"| `K`                                   | Strike ng option                                                                                              | 1 hanggang 2                                                   | 1.2 hanggang 1.8 (80% hanggang 120% ng spot price sa gitna ng domain, $S = 1.5$) |\n"
"| `w1` (basket ng 2 asset)              | Weight ng unang asset. Hinuhuha ang weight ng pangalawang asset: $w_2 = 1 - w_1$                              | Mahigpit na positibo ang bawat weight (kaya $0 < w_1 < 1$)     | Bawat weight mula 0.2 hanggang 0.8                                              |\n"
"| `w1`, `w2` (basket ng 3 asset)        | Mga weight ng una at ng pangalawang asset. Hinuhuha ang weight ng pangatlong asset: $w_3 = 1 - w_1 - w_2$    | Mahigpit na positibo ang bawat weight (kaya $w_1 + w_2 < 1$)   | Bawat isa sa tatlong weight mula 0.2 hanggang 0.8                               |\n"
"| `rho`, `rho12`, `rho13`, `rho23`      | Correlation ng dalawang asset                                                                                 | 0 hanggang 1 (dapat positive semi-definite ang correlation matrix) | 0.1 hanggang 0.8                                                            |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The range column gives the values accepted by the use case. The business range gives the values commonly met in practice: volatilities of equity indices, large capitalizations and currencies, strikes close to the spot price, moderate to high correlations between assets, and a residual maturity $T - t$ between 0.3 and 1 year.\n"
msgstr "Ibinibigay ng range column ang mga value na tinatanggap ng use case. Ibinibigay ng business range ang mga value na karaniwang nakikita sa praktika: mga volatility ng equity index, malalaking capitalization at currency, mga strike na malapit sa spot price, katamtaman hanggang mataas na correlation ng mga asset, at natitirang maturity na $T - t$ na nasa pagitan ng 0.3 at 1 taon.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The arguments for the Black-Scholes differential equations are on a fixed domain, as follows:\n"
msgstr "Ang mga argumento para sa mga differential equation ng Black-Scholes ay nasa isang fixed domain, tulad ng sumusunod:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "$t$ is between 0 and 0.9. The variable $x_i$ of each asset is between 0 and 1, and the price of the asset is $S_i = 1 + x_i$, so between 1 and 2.\n"
msgstr "Ang $t$ ay nasa pagitan ng 0 at 0.9. Ang variable na $x_i$ ng bawat asset ay nasa pagitan ng 0 at 1, at ang presyo ng asset ay $S_i = 1 + x_i$, kaya nasa pagitan ng 1 at 2.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Ansatz {#ansatz}"
msgstr "Ansatz {#ansatz}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The variable quantum circuit that encodes each function is selected with the `ansatz` argument:\n"
msgstr "Ang variational quantum circuit na nag-e-encode ng bawat function ay pinipili gamit ang argumentong `ansatz`:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`HEA` is a hardware-efficient ansatz measured with a global observable. It is the most general choice.\n"
msgstr "Ang `HEA` ay isang hardware-efficient ansatz na sinusukat gamit ang global na observable. Ito ang pinakapangkalahatang pagpipilian.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`BPM-LE` (Barren Plateau Mitigation, Low Expressivity) is an ansatz designed to avoid barren plateaus, measured with local observables. It has few parameters and shallow circuits, which keeps the cost of the optimization low, including the cost of parameter-shift gradients.\n"
msgstr "Ang `BPM-LE` (Barren Plateau Mitigation, Low Expressivity) ay isang ansatz na dinisenyo para iwasan ang mga barren plateau, na sinusukat gamit ang mga lokal na observable. Kaunti ang parameter nito at mababaw ang mga circuit, kaya mababa ang gastos ng optimization, kasama ang gastos ng mga parameter-shift gradient.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`BPM-HE` (Barren Plateau Mitigation, High Expressivity) follows the same construction with more parameters per circuit, for functions that the low-expressivity version cannot represent accurately enough.\n"
msgstr "Ang `BPM-HE` (Barren Plateau Mitigation, High Expressivity) ay sumusunod sa parehong konstruksyon pero mas maraming parameter bawat circuit, para sa mga function na hindi kayang katawanin nang sapat na tumpak ng low-expressivity na bersyon.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The number of qubits per variable and the depth of the circuit remain controlled by the `nb_qubits` and `depth` arguments.\n"
msgstr "Ang bilang ng qubit bawat variable at ang lalim ng circuit ay kinokontrol pa rin ng mga argumentong `nb_qubits` at `depth`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Optimizer chain and error metric {#optimizer-chain-and-error-metric}"
msgstr "Optimizer chain at error metric {#optimizer-chain-and-error-metric}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The optimizers are chained as a list of stages with the `optimizers` argument. Each stage defines its own method, its maximum number of iterations and its own number of shots, so that cheap and noisy evaluations explore the landscape first, and the number of shots increases as the optimization converges. A typical chain is made of the following pieces:\n"
msgstr "Ang mga optimizer ay pinag-uugnay bilang listahan ng mga stage gamit ang argumentong `optimizers`. Bawat stage ay may sariling method, sariling maximum na bilang ng iteration, at sariling bilang ng shot, kaya ang mura at maingay na mga evaluation ang unang nag-e-explore sa landscape, at dumadami ang bilang ng shot habang nagko-converge ang optimization. Ang karaniwang chain ay binubuo ng mga sumusunod na bahagi:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "One or more `CMAES` stages (global and gradient-free), which identify the right region of the space of solutions. Each stage has its own `shots`, `sigma0`, and `popsize` (population size, that is the number of candidates evaluated at each generation). The `sigma0` argument is the initial standard deviation of the search distribution of CMA-ES, that is, its initial step size: a large value widely explores the space of the circuit parameters, while a small value searches locally around the best candidate found so far. Decreasing `sigma0` from one stage to the next therefore moves from exploration to refinement.\n"
msgstr "Isa o higit pang `CMAES` stage (global at gradient-free), na tumutukoy sa tamang rehiyon ng espasyo ng mga solusyon. Bawat stage ay may sariling `shots`, `sigma0`, at `popsize` (laki ng populasyon, ibig sabihin ang bilang ng mga kandidatong ine-evaluate sa bawat henerasyon). Ang argumentong `sigma0` ay ang paunang standard deviation ng search distribution ng CMA-ES, ibig sabihin ang paunang laki ng hakbang nito: ang malaking value ay malawakang nag-e-explore sa espasyo ng mga parameter ng circuit, habang ang maliit na value ay naghahanap nang lokal sa paligid ng pinakamahusay na kandidatong nahanap pa lang. Kaya ang pagbaba ng `sigma0` mula sa isang stage patungo sa susunod ay paglipat mula sa exploration patungo sa refinement.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A `LS-TRF` stage (Least Squares - Trust Region Reflective), which explores this region to refine the final angles. Without `psr`, `LS-TRF` estimates the Jacobian of the cost function with finite differences. With `psr=True`, the Jacobian is computed on the QPU exactly, with the parameter-shift rule (PSR). The PSR increases the computation time since it requires additional circuits, but it allows a better precision than the finite differences.\n"
msgstr "Isang `LS-TRF` stage (Least Squares - Trust Region Reflective), na nag-e-explore sa rehiyong ito para pinuhin ang mga huling anggulo. Kung walang `psr`, tinatantya ng `LS-TRF` ang Jacobian ng cost function gamit ang finite differences. Kapag `psr=True`, kinukuwenta nang eksakto ang Jacobian sa QPU gamit ang parameter-shift rule (PSR). Pinapahaba ng PSR ang oras ng computation dahil kailangan nito ng karagdagang circuit, pero mas mataas ang precision nito kaysa sa finite differences.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The error metric used on this page is the Root Mean Square Error (RMSE) between the solution and the reference solution, over the sampled points. The function also reports the mean squared error (MSE) and the maximum absolute deviation, which are the d2 and d1 metrics of Section 2.6 of [the H-DES paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/2410.01130).\n"
msgstr "Ang error metric na ginagamit sa pahinang ito ay ang Root Mean Square Error (RMSE) sa pagitan ng solusyon at ng reference na solusyon, sa mga sampled na punto. Iniuulat din ng function ang mean squared error (MSE) at ang maximum absolute deviation, na siyang mga d2 at d1 metric ng Seksyon 2.6 ng [H-DES paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/2410.01130).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
