msgstr "Kasalukuyang bersyon {#current-version}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Example                                    | Total number of qubits | Ansatz   | RMSE                       | Classical compute time (min) | QPU time (min) |\n"
"| ------------------------------------------ | ---------------------- | -------- | -------------------------- | ---------------------------- | -------------- |\n"
"| Inviscid Burgers' equation                 | 4                      | `BPM-LE` | 0.0147                     | ~1                           | 11             |\n"
"| Pressureless Euler's equations             | 8                      | `HEA`    | 0.0193                     | ~1.5                         | 10             |\n"
"| Hypoelastic 1D tensile test                | 6                      | `HEA`    | 0.0296                     | ~1                           | 10             |\n"
"| Black-Scholes equation, 1 asset            | 6                      | `BPM-LE` | 0.0084                     | ~0.3                         | 5.0            |\n"
"| Black-Scholes equation, basket of 2 assets | 7                      | `BPM-HE` | 0.0085                     | ~4                           | 12.0           |\n"
"| Black-Scholes equation, basket of 3 assets | 9                      | `BPM-HE` | 0.0104                     | ~67                          | 20.7           |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Halimbawa                                  | Kabuuang bilang ng qubit | Ansatz   | RMSE                       | Classical compute time (min) | QPU time (min) |\n"
"| ------------------------------------------ | ---------------------- | -------- | -------------------------- | ---------------------------- | -------------- |\n"
"| Inviscid Burgers' equation                 | 4                      | `BPM-LE` | 0.0147                     | ~1                           | 11             |\n"
"| Pressureless Euler's equations             | 8                      | `HEA`    | 0.0193                     | ~1.5                         | 10             |\n"
"| Hypoelastic 1D tensile test                | 6                      | `HEA`    | 0.0296                     | ~1                           | 10             |\n"
"| Black-Scholes equation, 1 asset            | 6                      | `BPM-LE` | 0.0084                     | ~0.3                         | 5.0            |\n"
"| Black-Scholes equation, basket ng 2 asset | 7                      | `BPM-HE` | 0.0085                     | ~4                           | 12.0           |\n"
"| Black-Scholes equation, basket ng 3 asset | 9                      | `BPM-HE` | 0.0104                     | ~67                          | 20.7           |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The RMSE is the Root Mean Square Error between the solution and the reference solution (aggregated over the two functions for the Euler, and tensile test cases). For the Burgers, Euler, and tensile test cases, it is measured on the QPU over the sampled points. For the Black-Scholes cases, it is computed inside the domain, excluding the final time and the edges where the solution is imposed, on a fine grid (600 points per axis for 1 asset, 80 for 2 assets, 16 for 3 assets), by noiseless simulation at the parameters retained on the QPU. The classical compute time is the time spent by the optimizers on the classical side of the hybrid loop. It is mostly due to the evaluation of the points on the grid, which is easily parallelizable. The QPU time is the quantum processing time billed for the optimization jobs.\n"
msgstr "Ang RMSE ay ang Root Mean Square Error sa pagitan ng solusyon at ng reference na solusyon (pinagsama sa dalawang function para sa mga kaso ng Euler at tensile test). Para sa mga kaso ng Burgers, Euler, at tensile test, sinusukat ito sa QPU sa mga sampled na punto. Para sa mga kaso ng Black-Scholes, kinukuwenta ito sa loob ng domain, hindi isinasama ang huling oras at ang mga gilid kung saan ipinapataw ang solusyon, sa isang pinong grid (600 punto bawat axis para sa 1 asset, 80 para sa 2 asset, 16 para sa 3 asset), sa pamamagitan ng noiseless simulation sa mga parameter na nakuha sa QPU. Ang classical compute time ay ang oras na ginugol ng mga optimizer sa classical na bahagi ng hybrid loop. Karamihan nito ay dahil sa pag-evaluate ng mga punto sa grid, na madaling i-parallelize. Ang QPU time ay ang oras ng quantum processing na sinisingil para sa mga optimization job.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The number of qubits is lower than in the previous version. The circuit binding feature reduces the QPU time of the runs, not the number of qubits. It remains possible to increase the number of qubits by executing several circuits in parallel, which reduces the QPU time needed even further, and the new version of the function leaves room to scale to larger numbers of qubits and larger problems.\n"
msgstr "Mas mababa ang bilang ng qubit kaysa sa nakaraang bersyon. Binabawasan ng circuit binding feature ang QPU time ng mga takbo, hindi ang bilang ng qubit. Posible pa ring dagdagan ang bilang ng qubit sa pamamagitan ng pagpapatakbo ng ilang circuit nang magkasabay, na lalo pang nagpapababa sa kinakailangang QPU time, at nag-iiwan ang bagong bersyon ng function ng puwang para mag-scale sa mas malaking bilang ng qubit at mas malalaking problema.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The optimization steps of these runs are described as follows:\n"
"- The `popsize` argument is the number of candidates evaluated at each generation of `CMAES`.\n"
"- The `CMAES` stages can stop early when the cost stagnates.\n"
"- A cost evaluation is the computation of the cost function for one set of circuit parameters, measured on the QPU with the number of shots of the stage.\n"
"- A `CMAES` generation is made of `popsize` evaluations, so the iterations of `CMAES` are counted in generations.\n"
"- An `LS-TRF` iteration computes the Jacobian of the cost function at the current point, with the parameter-shift rule (PSR) here, and evaluates the cost function at one or several trial points.\n"
"- The Jacobian requires its own circuits (the parameter-shifted circuits), which are not counted as evaluations. The number of Jacobians is therefore the number of `LS-TRF` iterations, and the number of evaluations is higher than the number of iterations because some trial points are rejected.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang mga hakbang ng optimization ng mga takbong ito ay inilalarawan tulad ng sumusunod:\n"
"- Ang argumentong `popsize` ay ang bilang ng mga kandidatong ine-evaluate sa bawat henerasyon ng `CMAES`.\n"
"- Puwedeng huminto nang maaga ang mga `CMAES` stage kapag huminto ang pagbabago ng cost.\n"
"- Ang cost evaluation ay ang pagkuwenta ng cost function para sa isang set ng mga parameter ng circuit, na sinusukat sa QPU gamit ang bilang ng shot ng stage.\n"
"- Ang isang henerasyon ng `CMAES` ay binubuo ng `popsize` na mga evaluation, kaya ang mga iteration ng `CMAES` ay binibilang sa mga henerasyon.\n"
"- Ang isang iteration ng `LS-TRF` ay kumukuwenta ng Jacobian ng cost function sa kasalukuyang punto, gamit dito ang parameter-shift rule (PSR), at ine-evaluate ang cost function sa isa o higit pang trial point.\n"
"- Ang Jacobian ay nangangailangan ng sarili nitong mga circuit (ang mga parameter-shifted na circuit), na hindi binibilang bilang mga evaluation. Kaya ang bilang ng mga Jacobian ay ang bilang ng mga iteration ng `LS-TRF`, at mas mataas ang bilang ng mga evaluation kaysa sa bilang ng mga iteration dahil may mga trial point na tinatanggihan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Example                        | Stage | Method                   | Shots  | `sigma0` | `popsize` | Iterations                                 |\n"
"| ------------------------------ | ----- | ------------------------ | ------ | -------- | --------- | ------------------------------------------ |\n"
"| Inviscid Burgers' equation     | 1     | `CMAES`                  | 3,000  | 0.4      | 12        | 40 generations                             |\n"
"|                                | 2     | `CMAES`                  | 15,000 | 0.1      | 12        | 15 generations                             |\n"
"|                                | 3     | `CMAES`                  | 50,000 | 0.04     | 12        | 6 generations                              |\n"
"| Pressureless Euler's equations | 1     | `CMAES`                  | 2,500  | 0.5      | 12        | 12 generations                             |\n"
"|                                | 2     | `CMAES`                  | 4,000  | 0.15     | 12        | 18 generations                             |\n"
"|                                | 3     | `LS-TRF` with `psr=True` | 10,000 | n/a      | n/a       | 30 evaluations, 7 iterations (7 Jacobians) |\n"
"| Hypoelastic 1D tensile test    | 1     | `CMAES`                  | 2,500  | 0.5      | 12        | 12 generations                             |\n"
"|                                | 2     | `CMAES`                  | 4,000  | 0.15     | 12        | 18 generations                             |\n"
"|                                | 3     | `CMAES`                  | 6,000  | 0.07     | 12        | 12 generations                             |\n"
"|                                | 4     | `LS-TRF` with `psr=True` | 10,000 | n/a      | n/a       | 31 evaluations, 3 iterations (3 Jacobians) |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Halimbawa                      | Stage | Method                   | Shots  | `sigma0` | `popsize` | Mga iteration                              |\n"
"| ------------------------------ | ----- | ------------------------ | ------ | -------- | --------- | ------------------------------------------ |\n"
"| Inviscid Burgers' equation     | 1     | `CMAES`                  | 3,000  | 0.4      | 12        | 40 henerasyon                              |\n"
